  "note": "Election of the Newry Urban District Council, nominations taken 5 January 1932 (Newry Telegraph, 7 January 1932, p. 5). No ward was contested. Six nominated for six seats. Myles Connell's papers were declared invalid, leaving five valid nominations; as the outgoing councillor next in the 1929 poll he was declared re-elected to the sixth seat. McConville and McCaffrey are Nationalists, the other four Labour. Returned unopposed."
